+### Nushell
+
+Nushell has no completion scripts per command. It calls one external completer for every external command, with the
+words of the command line. The script that `nu_source` prints defines a command, `_foo_bar_completion`, that takes these
+words and returns the completions as records with a `value` and a `description` (the help text of an option or a
+command). Call it from your external completer for `foo-bar`:
+
+```nu
+$env.config.completions.external.enable = true
+$env.config.completions.external.completer = {|spans|
+    match $spans.0 {
+        foo-bar => { _foo_bar_completion $spans }
+        _ => null
+    }
+}
+```
+
+When a value is a file or a directory, the command returns `null`, and Nushell completes the path itself. The script
+needs Nushell 0.90 or newer; `nu_source` warns on stderr when an older `nu` is found.
 
 After modifying the shell config, you need to start a new shell in order for the changes to be loaded.
 
